# BLACKLIST, not whitelist. Inverted 2026-08-19.
#
# This file used to read `/*` followed by `!*.cc` and `!*.py`. That is a WHITELIST,
# and a whitelist FAILS CLOSED: every file type nobody thought to negate is
# invisible by default, permanently, and nothing surfaces it because there is
# nothing to see. It hid 13 shell scripts and 2 markdown files -- including
# run_full_pipeline.sh, run_generator.sh and launch_parallel.sh, which are the
# tooling that REGENERATES the ~16 GB of results deliberately excluded from this
# repository. Excluding generated data is only defensible while its generators
# ship; they were about to not ship.
#
# A blacklist fails OPEN: a missed output type shows up as a large file in
# `git status`, and publication_ready.sh already asserts no tracked file exceeds
# 45 MB. A missed source type under the old scheme showed up as nothing at all.
# That asymmetry is the whole argument for the inversion.
#
# Patterns below are taken from what the pipeline scripts actually write and
# delete (master_reset.sh:10,49,50 and run_full_pipeline.sh:47,51) -- classified
# by PRODUCER, not by file extension.

# --- generated simulation output -------------------------------------------
trace_*.csv
physics_scale_sweep_*.csv
*_out.txt

# --- generated dataset / training artefacts --------------------------------
geometric_training_dataset*.csv
split_index_*.npy
stage2_M*.pkl
stage2_result_M*.json

# --- editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# NOTE on lora-combining.cc / lora-dataset.cc: these were excluded here because
# they #include "ns3/lorawan-module.h" while src/lorawan was a nested third-party
# git repository with zero files tracked, so a clone got a scratch directory it
# could not compile -- and ns-3 builds every file in scratch/, so two unbuildable
# files block the whole tree. THAT PREMISE NO LONGER HOLDS: src/lorawan was
# vendored as 140 ordinary tracked files on 2026-08-19. The exclusion is therefore
# removed. Both files are currently ABSENT from the working tree; they exist in
# commit 2c1f888 and whether they should be restored is a question for the author.
